# Call-site ledger of anytree at 2e0a1b956172654d75aff93277ce3d883355e0bf.
# Hand-written from the source; judgements in anytree.md.
#
# Value sets used below (see anytree.md, "Value sets"):
#   nodes: a parameter that takes a tree node gets a node of the NodeMixin
#     family (NodeMixin, Node, AnyNode, SymlinkNodeMixin, SymlinkNode, client
#     subclasses) or of the LightNodeMixin family (LightNodeMixin, client
#     subclasses). A tree has nodes of one family: attaching a node to a
#     node of the other family raises AttributeError in __attach (judgement
#     J1). The calls before that failure count only where an isinstance
#     check of the package admits the other family: a LightNodeMixin node as
#     the value of NodeMixin.parent (nodemixin.py:122) and as a child given
#     to NodeMixin.children (nodemixin.py:230); then the NodeMixin node that
#     NodeMixin.children passes to LightNodeMixin.parent (lead, B2: an
#     isinstance check names the type for the role).
#   node reprs: repr() of a NodeMixin-family node runs Node.__repr__,
#     AnyNode.__repr__ or SymlinkNode.__repr__; LightNodeMixin and NodeMixin
#     define no __repr__.
#   SymlinkNode: its __getattr__ runs where normal lookup fails (an attribute
#     that lives in the target, such as name, or an unset _NodeMixin__parent
#     or _NodeMixin__children probed by hasattr); its __setattr__ runs for
#     every attribute assignment on it. The target of a SymlinkNode is a
#     NodeMixin-family node, also another SymlinkNode, never a
#     LightNodeMixin node (judgement J3; lead).
#   iterator filter_: AbstractIter.__default_filter (default), plus, for
#     PreOrderIter only, the filters the package passes: DotExporter._default_filter,
#     MermaidExporter.__iter__.<lambda1>, NodeMixin.leaves.<lambda1>,
#     LightNodeMixin.leaves.<lambda1>, search.findall_by_attr.<lambda1>,
#     search.find_by_attr.<lambda1>. iterator stop: AbstractIter.__default_stop,
#     plus MermaidExporter.__iter__.<lambda2> (passed to PreOrderIter).
default reject anytree.node.symlinknodemixin.SymlinkNodeMixin.__getattr__: the receiver is not a SymlinkNodeMixin instance (Python calls __getattr__ only on instances of classes that have it in their MRO), or it is one and normal lookup finds the attribute: a class attribute of NodeMixin or SymlinkNodeMixin (method, property, separator, __dict__, __class__) or an instance attribute that is set (target); a found NodeMixin property can still raise AttributeError through a client parent/child getter (R4-F1), and the affected concrete-SymlinkNode sites accept the fallback explicitly; the sites where a SymlinkNode can lack the attribute accept the candidate explicitly
default reject anytree.node.symlinknodemixin.SymlinkNodeMixin.__setattr__: the object whose attribute is assigned is not a SymlinkNodeMixin instance (an iterator, exporter, importer, style, resolver, exception, AnyNode, Node or LightNodeMixin); the sites where a SymlinkNode can be the object accept the candidate explicitly
default reject anytree.iterators.abstractiter.AbstractIter.__iter__, anytree.iterators.abstractiter.AbstractIter.__next__, anytree.render.RenderTree.__iter__, anytree.exporter.dotexporter.DotExporter.__iter__, anytree.exporter.mermaidexporter.MermaidExporter.__iter__: the iterated, unpacked, searched or converted value is a list, tuple, set, dict, dict view, str, generator, zip object or the *args/**kwargs of a call, never a tree iterator, RenderTree or exporter; the sites that iterate one accept the candidates explicitly
default reject anytree.render.RenderTree.__repr__, anytree.render.RenderTree.__str__: no package code converts, formats or compares a RenderTree; the operands are strs, ints, nodes, styles and client values
default reject anytree.render.AbstractStyle.__repr__: no package code formats a style except RenderTree.__repr__ ({self.style!r}), which accepts the candidate explicitly
default reject anytree.node.node.Node.__repr__, anytree.node.anynode.AnyNode.__repr__, anytree.node.symlinknode.SymlinkNode.__repr__: the converted or formatted value is not a node of the NodeMixin family (a str, int, None, a client value or a LightNodeMixin node, whose class has no package __repr__); the sites that format a node accept the candidates explicitly

